---
title: Reranking
id: rerank
order: 1
description: "Reorder candidate documents by relevance to a query with TanStack AI's rerank() API and the Cohere adapter — the precision step for RAG and search."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - rerank
  - reranking
  - relevance
  - rag
  - retrieval
  - semantic search
  - cohere
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a query and a list of candidate documents — chunks from a vector\nsearch, rows from a keyword query, FAQ entries — and you need them ordered by\nhow well they actually answer the query. Vector similarity gets you close, but\na dedicated reranking model is far more precise. By the end of this guide\nyou'll have that list reordered, with a relevance score per document."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the precision step in a retrieval pipeline: retrieve a broad set\nof candidates cheaply, then rerank to surface the few that matter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking is available from two adapters today:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-cohere"},{"type":"text","value":") — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')"},{"type":"text","value":", talking to Cohere directly."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":") — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5')"},{"type":"text","value":", routing rerank through your existing OpenRouter key."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both implement the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank()"},{"type":"text","value":" activity — swap the adapter, keep the call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Peer dependency:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"},{"type":"text","value":" and an array of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"documents"},{"type":"text","value":". The result's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerankedDocuments"},{"type":"text","value":"\nare ordered most-relevant first, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ranking"},{"type":"text","value":" carries the relevance score and\nthe original index of each."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking, rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\nconsole.log(ranking[0]) // { index: 1, score: 0.98, document: 'rainy afternoon in the city' }","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"COHERE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment. To pass a key\nexplicitly, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCohereRerank('rerank-v3.5', 'co-...')"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To rerank through OpenRouter instead, swap the adapter — everything else stays\nthe same:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openRouterRerank"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reranking-object-documents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking Object Documents"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Documents don't have to be strings. Pass JSON-serializable objects and the\noriginal object is returned in the result — fully typed — so you can carry an\nid or metadata through the rerank and read it back off the ranked results."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst chunks = [\n  { id: 'doc-1', text: 'A heavy gaming desktop with an RTX card.' },\n  { id: 'doc-2', text: 'A lightweight ultrabook with all-day battery.' },\n]\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'best laptop for travel',\n  documents: chunks,\n})\n\n// `document` is the original object — `id` is available and type-safe.\nconsole.log(ranking[0]?.document.id) // 'doc-2'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Object documents are serialized to JSON before being sent to the provider; the\nranking is mapped back to your original elements by index."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RerankAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A rerank adapter created with a model (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The search query documents are scored against — required"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"documents"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<string | object>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Candidate documents to rerank — required"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topN"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return only the top N results"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancel the in-flight request"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider options"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-specific options (see below)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<GenerationMiddleware>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"provider-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere rerank accepts:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'refund policy',\n  documents: ['Returns accepted within 30 days.', 'Free shipping over $50.'],\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Cap tokens kept per document when chunking long inputs (Cohere default: 4096).\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512,\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(ranking)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"result-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Shape"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { TokenUsage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RerankResult<TDocument = string> {\n  id: string\n  model: string\n  // Scored results, most relevant first.\n  ranking: Array<{ index: number; score: number; document: TDocument }>\n  // The documents reordered by relevance (ranking.map(r => r.document)).\n  rerankedDocuments: Array<TDocument>\n  // Rerank typically bills in provider \"search units\"\n  // (usage.billed = { quantity, unit: 'units' }). Some providers (for example\n  // OpenRouter) also report totalTokens and cost. Cohere reports only search\n  // units and leaves token counts at 0.\n  usage: TokenUsage\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-endpoint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Endpoint"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking runs on the server (it needs your API key). Wrap it in an API route\nand call it from the client over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/rerank.ts\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/rerank')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('query' in body) ||\n          typeof body.query !== 'string' ||\n          !('documents' in body) ||\n          !Array.isArray(body.documents)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { query, documents } = body\n        const topN = 'topN' in body && typeof body.topN === 'number'\n          ? body.topN\n          : undefined\n\n        const result = await rerank({\n          adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n          query,\n          documents,\n          topN,\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"// client.ts — call the endpoint and use the reordered documents\nasync function rerankDocuments(query: string, documents: Array<string>) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/rerank', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ query, documents, topN: 3 }),\n  })\n  const result = await res.json()\n  return result.rerankedDocuments\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"in-a-rag-pipeline","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In a RAG Pipeline"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking shines as the second stage after a cheap, broad retrieval. Over-fetch\ncandidates with vector search, then rerank to keep only the most relevant few\nfor the prompt:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { vectorSearch } from './my-vector-store'\n\nasync function retrieveContext(query: string) {\n  // 1. Over-fetch candidates cheaply.\n  const candidates = await vectorSearch(query, { limit: 50 })\n\n  // 2. Rerank and keep the most relevant handful for the prompt.\n  const { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query,\n    documents: candidates.map((c) => c.text),\n    topN: 5,\n  })\n\n  return rerankedDocuments\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cancellation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancellation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" to cancel an in-flight request:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation — the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" contract the media activities\nuse:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        if (usage.billed) {\n          console.log(\n            `search units billed: ${usage.billed.quantity} ${usage.billed.unit}`,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tip:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware()"},{"type":"text","value":" to emit OpenTelemetry spans for rerank\ncalls. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/otel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenTelemetry"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Cohere rerank adapter uses:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"COHERE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":": Your Cohere API key"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query: 'q',\n    documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  })\n  console.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Rerank failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing an empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"documents"},{"type":"text","value":" array throws before any request is made."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"runnable-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runnable Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-rerank"},{"type":"text","value":" is a small TanStack Start app that runs everything\non this page: a fixed corpus of support articles listed newest-first, a query\nbox, and a side-by-side view of the original order against the reranked order\nwith scores. The provider dropdown switches between the Cohere and OpenRouter\nadapters over the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank()"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"code","value":"cd examples/ts-react-rerank\npnpm install\ncp .env.example .env   # add COHERE_API_KEY and/or OPENROUTER_API_KEY\npnpm dev","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/cohere","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — models, configuration, and explicit API keys"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openrouter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — rerank through your OpenRouter key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — lifecycle hooks for usage and errors"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"providers","text":"Providers","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"reranking-object-documents","text":"Reranking Object Documents","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"provider-options","text":"Provider Options","level":3},{"id":"result-shape","text":"Result Shape","level":2},{"id":"server-endpoint","text":"Server Endpoint","level":2},{"id":"in-a-rag-pipeline","text":"In a RAG Pipeline","level":2},{"id":"cancellation","text":"Cancellation","level":2},{"id":"observability","text":"Observability","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":2},{"id":"runnable-example","text":"Runnable Example","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a query and a list of candidate documents — chunks from a vector\nsearch, rows from a keyword query, FAQ entries — and you need them ordered by\nhow well they actually answer the query. Vector similarity gets you close, but\na dedicated reranking model is far more precise. By the end of this guide\nyou'll have that list reordered, with a relevance score per document.\n\n`rerank()` is the precision step in a retrieval pipeline: retrieve a broad set\nof candidates cheaply, then rerank to surface the few that matter.\n\n## Providers\n\nReranking is available from two adapters today:\n\n- **Cohere** (`@tanstack/ai-cohere`) — `cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')`, talking to Cohere directly.\n- **OpenRouter** (`@tanstack/ai-openrouter`) — `openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5')`, routing rerank through your existing OpenRouter key.\n\nBoth implement the same `rerank()` activity — swap the adapter, keep the call.\n\n## Installation\n\nCohere:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvue: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-cohere\npreact: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nangular: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-cohere\noctane: @tanstack/ai-cohere\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nOpenRouter:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai\nvue: @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai\npreact: @tanstack/ai\nangular: @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai\noctane: @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nPass a `query` and an array of `documents`. The result's `rerankedDocuments`\nare ordered most-relevant first, and `ranking` carries the relevance score and\nthe original index of each.\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking, rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\nconsole.log(ranking[0]) // { index: 1, score: 0.98, document: 'rainy afternoon in the city' }\n```\n\nThe adapter reads `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment. To pass a key\nexplicitly, use `createCohereRerank('rerank-v3.5', 'co-...')`.\n\nTo rerank through OpenRouter instead, swap the adapter — everything else stays\nthe same:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\n```\n\n`openRouterRerank` reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n## Reranking Object Documents\n\nDocuments don't have to be strings. Pass JSON-serializable objects and the\noriginal object is returned in the result — fully typed — so you can carry an\nid or metadata through the rerank and read it back off the ranked results.\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst chunks = [\n  { id: 'doc-1', text: 'A heavy gaming desktop with an RTX card.' },\n  { id: 'doc-2', text: 'A lightweight ultrabook with all-day battery.' },\n]\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'best laptop for travel',\n  documents: chunks,\n})\n\n// `document` is the original object — `id` is available and type-safe.\nconsole.log(ranking[0]?.document.id) // 'doc-2'\n```\n\nObject documents are serialized to JSON before being sent to the provider; the\nranking is mapped back to your original elements by index.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option        | Type                          | Description                                                              |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `adapter`     | `RerankAdapter`               | A rerank adapter created with a model (e.g. `cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')`) |\n| `query`       | `string`                      | The search query documents are scored against — required                |\n| `documents`   | `Array<string \\| object>`     | Candidate documents to rerank — required                                 |\n| `topN`        | `number`                      | Return only the top N results                                            |\n| `abortSignal` | `AbortSignal`                 | Cancel the in-flight request                                             |\n| `modelOptions`| provider options              | Provider-specific options (see below)                                    |\n| `middleware`  | `Array<GenerationMiddleware>` | Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)               |\n\n### Provider Options\n\nCohere rerank accepts:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'refund policy',\n  documents: ['Returns accepted within 30 days.', 'Free shipping over $50.'],\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Cap tokens kept per document when chunking long inputs (Cohere default: 4096).\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512,\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(ranking)\n```\n\n## Result Shape\n\n```typescript\nimport type { TokenUsage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RerankResult<TDocument = string> {\n  id: string\n  model: string\n  // Scored results, most relevant first.\n  ranking: Array<{ index: number; score: number; document: TDocument }>\n  // The documents reordered by relevance (ranking.map(r => r.document)).\n  rerankedDocuments: Array<TDocument>\n  // Rerank typically bills in provider \"search units\"\n  // (usage.billed = { quantity, unit: 'units' }). Some providers (for example\n  // OpenRouter) also report totalTokens and cost. Cohere reports only search\n  // units and leaves token counts at 0.\n  usage: TokenUsage\n}\n```\n\n## Server Endpoint\n\nReranking runs on the server (it needs your API key). Wrap it in an API route\nand call it from the client over `fetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/rerank.ts\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/rerank')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('query' in body) ||\n          typeof body.query !== 'string' ||\n          !('documents' in body) ||\n          !Array.isArray(body.documents)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { query, documents } = body\n        const topN = 'topN' in body && typeof body.topN === 'number'\n          ? body.topN\n          : undefined\n\n        const result = await rerank({\n          adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n          query,\n          documents,\n          topN,\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// client.ts — call the endpoint and use the reordered documents\nasync function rerankDocuments(query: string, documents: Array<string>) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/rerank', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ query, documents, topN: 3 }),\n  })\n  const result = await res.json()\n  return result.rerankedDocuments\n}\n```\n\n## In a RAG Pipeline\n\nReranking shines as the second stage after a cheap, broad retrieval. Over-fetch\ncandidates with vector search, then rerank to keep only the most relevant few\nfor the prompt:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { vectorSearch } from './my-vector-store'\n\nasync function retrieveContext(query: string) {\n  // 1. Over-fetch candidates cheaply.\n  const candidates = await vectorSearch(query, { limit: 50 })\n\n  // 2. Rerank and keep the most relevant handful for the prompt.\n  const { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query,\n    documents: candidates.map((c) => c.text),\n    topN: 5,\n  })\n\n  return rerankedDocuments\n}\n```\n\n## Cancellation\n\nPass an `abortSignal` to cancel an in-flight request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n```\n\n## Observability\n\nAttach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation — the same `GenerationMiddleware` contract the media activities\nuse:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        if (usage.billed) {\n          console.log(\n            `search units billed: ${usage.billed.quantity} ${usage.billed.unit}`,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Pass `otelMiddleware()` to emit OpenTelemetry spans for rerank\n> calls. See [OpenTelemetry](../advanced/otel).\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nThe Cohere rerank adapter uses:\n\n- `COHERE_API_KEY`: Your Cohere API key\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query: 'q',\n    documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  })\n  console.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Rerank failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> Passing an empty `documents` array throws before any request is made.\n\n## Runnable Example\n\n`examples/ts-react-rerank` is a small TanStack Start app that runs everything\non this page: a fixed corpus of support articles listed newest-first, a query\nbox, and a side-by-side view of the original order against the reranked order\nwith scores. The provider dropdown switches between the Cohere and OpenRouter\nadapters over the same `rerank()` call.\n\n```bash\ncd examples/ts-react-rerank\npnpm install\ncp .env.example .env   # add COHERE_API_KEY and/or OPENROUTER_API_KEY\npnpm dev\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Cohere Adapter](../adapters/cohere) — models, configuration, and explicit API keys\n- [OpenRouter Adapter](../adapters/openrouter) — rerank through your OpenRouter key\n- [Middleware](../advanced/middleware) — lifecycle hooks for usage and errors\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Reranking\nid: rerank\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Reorder candidate documents by relevance to a query with TanStack AI's rerank() API and the Cohere adapter — the precision step for RAG and search.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - rerank\n  - reranking\n  - relevance\n  - rag\n  - retrieval\n  - semantic search\n  - cohere\n---\n\nYou have a query and a list of candidate documents — chunks from a vector\nsearch, rows from a keyword query, FAQ entries — and you need them ordered by\nhow well they actually answer the query. Vector similarity gets you close, but\na dedicated reranking model is far more precise. By the end of this guide\nyou'll have that list reordered, with a relevance score per document.\n\n`rerank()` is the precision step in a retrieval pipeline: retrieve a broad set\nof candidates cheaply, then rerank to surface the few that matter.\n\n## Providers\n\nReranking is available from two adapters today:\n\n- **Cohere** (`@tanstack/ai-cohere`) — `cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')`, talking to Cohere directly.\n- **OpenRouter** (`@tanstack/ai-openrouter`) — `openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5')`, routing rerank through your existing OpenRouter key.\n\nBoth implement the same `rerank()` activity — swap the adapter, keep the call.\n\n## Installation\n\nCohere:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvue: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-cohere\npreact: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nangular: @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-cohere\noctane: @tanstack/ai-cohere\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nOpenRouter:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openrouter\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai\nvue: @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai\npreact: @tanstack/ai\nangular: @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai\noctane: @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nPass a `query` and an array of `documents`. The result's `rerankedDocuments`\nare ordered most-relevant first, and `ranking` carries the relevance score and\nthe original index of each.\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking, rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\nconsole.log(ranking[0]) // { index: 1, score: 0.98, document: 'rainy afternoon in the city' }\n```\n\nThe adapter reads `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment. To pass a key\nexplicitly, use `createCohereRerank('rerank-v3.5', 'co-...')`.\n\nTo rerank through OpenRouter instead, swap the adapter — everything else stays\nthe same:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: openRouterRerank('cohere/rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'talk about rain',\n  documents: ['sunny day at the beach', 'rainy afternoon in the city'],\n  topN: 2,\n})\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]) // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\n```\n\n`openRouterRerank` reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n## Reranking Object Documents\n\nDocuments don't have to be strings. Pass JSON-serializable objects and the\noriginal object is returned in the result — fully typed — so you can carry an\nid or metadata through the rerank and read it back off the ranked results.\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst chunks = [\n  { id: 'doc-1', text: 'A heavy gaming desktop with an RTX card.' },\n  { id: 'doc-2', text: 'A lightweight ultrabook with all-day battery.' },\n]\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'best laptop for travel',\n  documents: chunks,\n})\n\n// `document` is the original object — `id` is available and type-safe.\nconsole.log(ranking[0]?.document.id) // 'doc-2'\n```\n\nObject documents are serialized to JSON before being sent to the provider; the\nranking is mapped back to your original elements by index.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option        | Type                          | Description                                                              |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `adapter`     | `RerankAdapter`               | A rerank adapter created with a model (e.g. `cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5')`) |\n| `query`       | `string`                      | The search query documents are scored against — required                |\n| `documents`   | `Array<string \\| object>`     | Candidate documents to rerank — required                                 |\n| `topN`        | `number`                      | Return only the top N results                                            |\n| `abortSignal` | `AbortSignal`                 | Cancel the in-flight request                                             |\n| `modelOptions`| provider options              | Provider-specific options (see below)                                    |\n| `middleware`  | `Array<GenerationMiddleware>` | Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)               |\n\n### Provider Options\n\nCohere rerank accepts:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'refund policy',\n  documents: ['Returns accepted within 30 days.', 'Free shipping over $50.'],\n  modelOptions: {\n    // Cap tokens kept per document when chunking long inputs (Cohere default: 4096).\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512,\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(ranking)\n```\n\n## Result Shape\n\n```typescript\nimport type { TokenUsage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RerankResult<TDocument = string> {\n  id: string\n  model: string\n  // Scored results, most relevant first.\n  ranking: Array<{ index: number; score: number; document: TDocument }>\n  // The documents reordered by relevance (ranking.map(r => r.document)).\n  rerankedDocuments: Array<TDocument>\n  // Rerank typically bills in provider \"search units\"\n  // (usage.billed = { quantity, unit: 'units' }). Some providers (for example\n  // OpenRouter) also report totalTokens and cost. Cohere reports only search\n  // units and leaves token counts at 0.\n  usage: TokenUsage\n}\n```\n\n## Server Endpoint\n\nReranking runs on the server (it needs your API key). Wrap it in an API route\nand call it from the client over `fetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/rerank.ts\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/rerank')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('query' in body) ||\n          typeof body.query !== 'string' ||\n          !('documents' in body) ||\n          !Array.isArray(body.documents)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { query, documents } = body\n        const topN = 'topN' in body && typeof body.topN === 'number'\n          ? body.topN\n          : undefined\n\n        const result = await rerank({\n          adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n          query,\n          documents,\n          topN,\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// client.ts — call the endpoint and use the reordered documents\nasync function rerankDocuments(query: string, documents: Array<string>) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/rerank', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ query, documents, topN: 3 }),\n  })\n  const result = await res.json()\n  return result.rerankedDocuments\n}\n```\n\n## In a RAG Pipeline\n\nReranking shines as the second stage after a cheap, broad retrieval. Over-fetch\ncandidates with vector search, then rerank to keep only the most relevant few\nfor the prompt:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\nimport { vectorSearch } from './my-vector-store'\n\nasync function retrieveContext(query: string) {\n  // 1. Over-fetch candidates cheaply.\n  const candidates = await vectorSearch(query, { limit: 50 })\n\n  // 2. Rerank and keep the most relevant handful for the prompt.\n  const { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query,\n    documents: candidates.map((c) => c.text),\n    topN: 5,\n  })\n\n  return rerankedDocuments\n}\n```\n\n## Cancellation\n\nPass an `abortSignal` to cancel an in-flight request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n```\n\n## Observability\n\nAttach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation — the same `GenerationMiddleware` contract the media activities\nuse:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\nconst result = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n  query: 'q',\n  documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        if (usage.billed) {\n          console.log(\n            `search units billed: ${usage.billed.quantity} ${usage.billed.unit}`,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Pass `otelMiddleware()` to emit OpenTelemetry spans for rerank\n> calls. See [OpenTelemetry](../advanced/otel).\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nThe Cohere rerank adapter uses:\n\n- `COHERE_API_KEY`: Your Cohere API key\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { cohereRerank } from '@tanstack/ai-cohere'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await rerank({\n    adapter: cohereRerank('rerank-v3.5'),\n    query: 'q',\n    documents: ['a', 'b'],\n  })\n  console.log(result.rerankedDocuments)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Rerank failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> Passing an empty `documents` array throws before any request is made.\n\n## Runnable Example\n\n`examples/ts-react-rerank` is a small TanStack Start app that runs everything\non this page: a fixed corpus of support articles listed newest-first, a query\nbox, and a side-by-side view of the original order against the reranked order\nwith scores. The provider dropdown switches between the Cohere and OpenRouter\nadapters over the same `rerank()` call.\n\n```bash\ncd examples/ts-react-rerank\npnpm install\ncp .env.example .env   # add COHERE_API_KEY and/or OPENROUTER_API_KEY\npnpm dev\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Cohere Adapter](../adapters/cohere) — models, configuration, and explicit API keys\n- [OpenRouter Adapter](../adapters/openrouter) — rerank through your OpenRouter key\n- [Middleware](../advanced/middleware) — lifecycle hooks for usage and errors\n"}
